When we make a new release (create a release-* tag or and a version-* branch),

The build stage should be built automatically, and mandatory.
(build:alfe:windows build:alfe:macos)

The test stage should be built automatically:
- all the build: jobs (shouldn't it be moved to the build stage?)
- all the test: jobs,
- all the verify: jobs,
are mandatory.

The benchmark stage should be built automatically:
- all the benchmark job are pass if fail.

The release stage should be built automatically:
- all the release jobs are mandatory.

The collect stage should be built automatically:
- all the collect jobs are mandatory.

The deploy stage should be built automatically:
- all the deploy jobs are mandatory.

== Resolution (2026-07-29) ==

Implemented in .gitlab-ci.yml.

- workflow now also triggers on =version-*= pointer branches (release-*
  tags already triggered).
- Two rule anchors define the "release ref" condition
  (=$CI_COMMIT_TAG =~ /^release-[0-9]/ || $CI_COMMIT_BRANCH =~ /^version-/=):
  =*on-release-mandatory= (when: on_success, allow_failure: false) and
  =*on-release-benchmark= (allow_failure: true). Each is spliced as the FIRST
  rule of the relevant template/job so a release ref wins over the manual
  fallback; off a release ref the existing rules (manual CAD lanes, automatic
  poseidon lanes) are unchanged.
- build stage: =.alfe-build= (build:alfe:windows/macos) mandatory on release;
  =build:alfe:sbcl= MOVED from the test stage to the build stage (answering
  the "shouldn't it be in build?" question — every =build:*= job is now in
  the build stage; build:clautolisp-ci-image stays build, and deliberately
  does NOT rebuild on a release tag, using the published :latest).
- test stage mandatory on release: =.platform-test-common=
  (test:clautolisp:macos/windows), =.verify-registry-common= (verify:*),
  =.vendor-probe-common= (vendor:probes:*). The plain =test:*= poseidon lanes
  had no rules and were already automatic + mandatory. =.encoding-experiment=
  is measurement, left auto + allow_failure (not a gate).
- benchmark stage: =.benchmark= / =.benchmark-cad= auto + allow_failure on
  release (pass-if-fail), per the issue.
- release / collect / deploy stages mandatory on release: =.release-common=,
  =collect:release=, =pages=, =deploy:documentation= (their old
  release-[0-9]-tag-only clause is replaced by the anchor, which also covers
  version-* branches and pins allow_failure: false).

Validated with =glab ci lint= (valid).

NOTES / follow-ups:
- Because BOTH the release-* tag and the version-* branches are release
  triggers, a release that pushes =release-1.7.0 + version-1.7 + version-1=
  in one go creates THREE pipelines, each running the full mandatory
  pipeline (incl. the CAD build/test lanes). If that is too heavy on the
  intermittent runners, restrict release/collect/deploy (or all of it) to the
  tag only. Left as specified for now.
- test:clautolisp:macos is now MANDATORY on a release, and it currently
  fails on a pre-existing macOS-only bug
  (vl-directory-filename-helpers-fail-macos.issue) — so a release pipeline
  will be red until that is fixed. That is the intended effect of mandatory
  release verification (it surfaces the real bug).
